# Line endings are load-bearing here.
#
# A shell script checked out with CRLF fails on Mac and Linux with the
# baffling error "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", so the launchers are
# pinned to LF regardless of the platform or the user's core.autocrlf
# setting. The Windows batch file is pinned to CRLF for the same reason in
# reverse: cmd.exe mishandles a .bat file with bare LF line endings.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.command   text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf

*.bat       text eol=crlf

# The prose corpus is the training text for the language model. Keep it
# plain and diffable.
src/cipher_tool/data/*.txt text eol=lf
